<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>French high school blockades to restart on Monday, student unions say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d02e71928e89a0d47431c920205adbb97c6632a1bbb0eda08d632204e7985ace</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:19:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T14:31:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261101-french-high-school-blockades-to-restart-on-monday-student-unions-say--68f8a87c0bfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261101-french-high-school-blockades-to-restart-on-monday-student-unions-say" /><summary type="html">The head of a student union said Sunday that high school blockades throughout France would restart on Monday. French President Emmanuel Macron has called for classes to resume after the government announced new measures to address the ongoing education crisis which student groups found insufficient.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Democrats face leftward surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8da63dde22abfc410642efcb8a3972f2b5daf6c2a2f03675622d446ff8d2bc9</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:19:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:56:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge--a5f145f073e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge" /><summary type="html">As Democrats seek to regain control of Congress, divisions within the party are emerging over its future direction. A new wave of progressive candidates is pushing to shift priorities further to the left, challenging corporate money in politics and calling for universal healthcare, climate action and an end to police violence. Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland rocked by Constitutional showdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b09f0a86223af174e94e981789f479840e1899a92e6009bd637a30287115e61</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:19:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:41:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown--f25dbb628a78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown" /><summary type="html">Poland’s constitutional crisis deepened on Saturday as the European Commission urged President Karol Nawrocki to recognise new judges appointed by Prime Minister Donald Tusk. The standoff comes ahead of next year’s parliamentary election, with polls suggesting a close race between Tusk’s coalition and the nationalist right. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Route du Rhum fleet ready to depart</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7755ab668705bfed8cbeffd6381c2784ab54ce1cc17d7f1728cf6860e231faa</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:19:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:12:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-route-du-rhum-fleet-ready-to-depart--0e53231c836e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-route-du-rhum-fleet-ready-to-depart" /><summary type="html">The Route du Rhum, billed as the world’s biggest solo transatlantic race, is set to depart from Saint-Malo in Brittany. Skippers will sail alone to Guadeloupe, with professionals and amateur sailors competing in the race, held every four years. Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Lula's victory, Israeli elections and Spain train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d938a26e2a0138792251a71be161c8267a2000ab65c72601070e9eab7f508a40</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T11:14:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-the-week-in-pictures-lula-s-victory-israeli-elections-and-spain-train-crash--07ac9159f69c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-the-week-in-pictures-lula-s-victory-israeli-elections-and-spain-train-crash" /><summary type="html">From Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's reelection in Brazil's presidential polls, to razor-sharp margins in the Israeli general elections, to a deadly high-speed train collision in Spain, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>A day of celebration in Senegal as the Youth Olympic Games get underway</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0d6dbfcf5aa068f0284abe8e7e5f9ff09e210afede24a3ecd5157398ccb92f0</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T11:14:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261101-a-day-of-celebration-in-senegal-as-the-youth-olympic-games-get-underway--0b51841f705c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261101-a-day-of-celebration-in-senegal-as-the-youth-olympic-games-get-underway" /><summary type="html">It is a historic day for Africa and Senegal. For the first time ever, an Olympic competition is being held on African soil. The Youth Olympic Games officially got underway in Senegal in the Dakar region on Saturday, with an opening ceremony attended by 30,000 people. The competition, which brings together 2,700 athletes aged between 14 and 17, will take place across three Senegalese cities, with 25 sports on the programme.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal hosts first Olympic event on African continent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bbbd6d04046d1aefebf3b281f8f59768ddaa24c9d079691a72dda98b6297d0e</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:58:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/senegal-hosts-first-olympic-event-on-african-continent--b512a9a9b84e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/senegal-hosts-first-olympic-event-on-african-continent" /><summary type="html">Youth Olympics make history with first African Games in over 130 years, opened by Senegal’s president in Dakar. 136 Senegalese athletes are competing, supported by 6,000 local volunteers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Youth Olympic Games kick off in Dakar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77f41bef8ca50b8959f698ddd9cdfe812e0681e114c674145b74730846d94ad2</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:49:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-kick-off-in-dakar--423e308b5a0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-kick-off-in-dakar" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Youth Olympic Games have officially kicked off in Senegal. Crowds gathered for Saturday's opening ceremony, featuring hundreds of drummers and dancers celebrating Senegalese and wider African culture, in keeping with the Games' motto: “Africa welcomes, Dakar celebrates”. It is the first-ever Olympic sporting event to be held on the African continent, but comes as Senegal faces an economic crisis. The country's president has said he wants to turn sport into an “economic and social engine”. The Games also come amid a government crackdown on LGBTQ+ people. Nearly 3,000 teenagers from more than 200 countries are competing in around a dozen sports, including athletics, beach wrestling and a five-a-side version of baseball. Jean-Loup Chappelet, Professor at Lausanne University and Olympics specialist, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>The World celebrates Halloween: Traditions, costumes and pumpkins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:081bf760c135ff651d20e32e87e032b7f54547416b3ccd02bee55b1fd0680377</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:43:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261101-the-world-celebrates-halloween-traditions-costumes-and-pumpkins--cff8ce62b6c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261101-the-world-celebrates-halloween-traditions-costumes-and-pumpkins" /><summary type="html">Halloween celebrations have been embraced in many countries around the world. Charlotte Hughes brings us this round-up.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: 115 yachts will sail out of Sain-Malo for Route du Rhum race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0edbac5a41938b9d15996df6524c0cc664480febadd90679ae89abd8eadbee96</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:40:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-115-yachts-will-sail-out-of-sain-malo-for-route-du-rhum-race--411dbf756fef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-115-yachts-will-sail-out-of-sain-malo-for-route-du-rhum-race" /><summary type="html">In Saint-Malo, in France's Brittany region, the legendary Route du Rhum is preparing to set sail. Billed as the world's biggest solo transatlantic race, it sees skippers sail alone from France's northern coast to the Caribbean island of Guadeloupe. It's a high-speed, high-risk crossing that takes place every four years.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Affordability at heart of Michigan race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0de3e06e4bc4fcf2b299fc2192d4af9d441f0250f7b88f265d989ede592388f7</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:39:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-affordability-at-heart-of-michigan-race--ad6ada0d04e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-affordability-at-heart-of-michigan-race" /><summary type="html">For many voters, the cost of living is the single biggest issue. Our reporters Jessica Le Masurier and Sarah Andersen travelled to Michigan to meet voters, where, according to one NGO, around 40% of the population struggle to afford basic necessities.</summary></entry><entry><title>Youth-led rallies sweep Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a67e92a1d0740001a771071062795ab6777fe250ba040107af8765f638bb92</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe--7747234b0c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe" /><summary type="html">Protests in France have helped inspire youth demonstrations elsewhere in Europe, from Portugal and Italy to Germany. Germany saw particularly large rallies on Saturday, led by a youth initiative whose name roughly translates as “Gen Z has got this”. Demonstrators called for better education and healthcare, stronger climate protection and a more affordable cost of living, while also opposing any return to compulsory military service. However, protests in several major German cities turned violent towards the end of the day, particularly in the financial hub of Frankfurt. Charlotte Hughes reports on the demonstrations across Europe.</summary></entry><entry><title>How social media are central to protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82d82bd669c90015c29ba4798989f4eab17fa723587929f1add3f1e416dfd252</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:36:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/how-social-media-are-central-to-protests--4b788fd2189b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/how-social-media-are-central-to-protests" /><summary type="html">As we saw in that report, protesters were frustrated at being kept on the outskirts of the French capital. There are also reports of social media posts about the demonstrations being suppressed. Daniel Quinlan has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of thousands protest in France for "Act III"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72e74caed8b6b154b164f15f9043e192004bd5a7de9b505016780b043d8e17b0</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:35:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hundreds-of-thousands-protest-in-france-for-act-iii--b4142750d323.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hundreds-of-thousands-protest-in-france-for-act-iii" /><summary type="html">A heavy police presence was hard to miss on the streets of Paris on Saturday, as the capital saw demonstrations for a third consecutive weekend over the rising cost of living and deteriorating conditions in schools. But the increased security failed to prevent clashes in several parts of the city. Riot police fired tear gas to push back protesters, while small fires broke out in several areas. Similar scenes unfolded across the country, including in Bordeaux, Toulouse and Marseille. Still, the demonstrations were largely less violent than the chaos witnessed on October 17. Caroline Baum has this round-up of the day's events.</summary></entry><entry><title>Binance resumes crypto withdrawals after major hack blamed on North Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f927c90e9fa80823524a86952e65f33e6526b168d488c1446ec12ce37bd9db3</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T07:01:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/business/20261101-binance-says-resuming-withdrawals-after-major-hack--a0ed2b42df7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/business/20261101-binance-says-resuming-withdrawals-after-major-hack" /><summary type="html">Binance, the world’s biggest cryptocurrency exchange, on Sunday said it would resume withdrawals after a suspension due to a major hack, which the FBI has tied ​to North Korea. The exchange said it covered 95% of the $6.3 billion in tokens stolen from its platform in the world's largest digital heist.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Indian opposition parties stage mega rally seeking election chief’s resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92a345f271d0d7f1ab900adba2ac8e16a3c13e4b61a22a2dd1321e119950f932</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T06:24:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261101-india-tightens-security-as-opposition-holds-mega-rally-demanding-election-chief-s-resignati--cf6cc8f746e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261101-india-tightens-security-as-opposition-holds-mega-rally-demanding-election-chief-s-resignation" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of demonstrators on Sunday joined a protest in New Delhi called by Indian opposition leader Rahul Gandhi and backed by the youth “Cockroach” movement amid tight security. Protesters are demanding the resignation of the country's election chief over voter list revisions that critics say favour Prime Minister Narendra Modi's party.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgarians vote in presidential runoff amid security tensions in the Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7574fe5bdf941ecdc5ab751ea0274ccaf90b4042f73c39f8112b586882cdd1fd</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T05:47:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-bulgarians-vote-in-presidential-runoff-amid-security-tensions-in-the-black-sea--8b2d7985fd75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-bulgarians-vote-in-presidential-runoff-amid-security-tensions-in-the-black-sea" /><summary type="html">Bulgarians voted Sunday in a presidential runoff between two candidates with opposing views on the Ukraine war and relations with Russia as tensions mount in the Black Sea. Incumbent President Iliana Iotova, who favours dialogue with Moscow, faces off against Andrey Gyurov, a former caretaker prime minister backed by the pro-Western opposition.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Testimonies from Oleshky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ae145abb9745abbfb98a04a64fe7f35aab2847615149cfacba803adedff9da7</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T23:54:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261031-testimonies-from-oleshky--738a0891e290.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261031-testimonies-from-oleshky" /><summary type="html">American Filmmaker Zarina Zabrisky has lived and reported across the Dnipro River in Ukrainian controlled Kherson for the past three years. She’s been speaking to France 24’s Gavin Lee about the events of the past 24 hours.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Some 320,000 demonstrators take part in largely peaceful protests across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa69cbee46fe1fd29b9aee0db319c27918a77fff3206dddf081849158bbc43fd</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T21:34:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261031-some-320-000-demonstrators-take-part-in-largely-peaceful-protests-across-france--d9fbf0865a48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261031-some-320-000-demonstrators-take-part-in-largely-peaceful-protests-across-france" /><summary type="html">Around 320,000 protesters took part in a third mass protest over living costs across France on Saturday, the interior ministry estimated, while organisers counted nearly half a million. Tensions flared ​at the end of marches in ​some cities but authorities reported that most demonstrations were largely peaceful.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>'Gen Z' demonstrations across Germany demand more education funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:030a98c521654b9abc349a8aca96eb0e34dfcae1538c8231a97e65a26a1fcb6d</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T20:07:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-german-police-protesters-clash-after-gen-z-demos--1625df057110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-german-police-protesters-clash-after-gen-z-demos" /><summary type="html">Police and protesters clashed Saturday in Germany where tens of thousands of young people took to the streets, inspired by similar movements in other European countries. Organized by the "GenZ regelt!" ("Gen Z has got this!") group, marches were held nationwide to demand more funding for education and to protest the high cost of living.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Senegal kicks off Africa's first ever Olympics with Youth Games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6654e8557757bfdd49b00f3946cc178bfe5d5e1e3ca8ba59ee63a53ea0a193c</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T19:15:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261031-senegal-hosts-africa-s-first-ever-youth-olympic-games--48359a071e4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261031-senegal-hosts-africa-s-first-ever-youth-olympic-games" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's Khamenei warns US and Israel against new attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:643e5e45fd50141542536c374fb7bf2a1aeb0d0b50b0227c42aa1b66b7c1d52e</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T17:00:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261031-iran-s-khamenei-warns-us-and-israel-against-new-attacks--ffe715e07f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261031-iran-s-khamenei-warns-us-and-israel-against-new-attacks" /><summary type="html">Iran's supreme leader warned the United States and Israel on Saturday against further strikes as tensions mount over a possible return to fighting. US President Donald Trump and Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu have threatened new military action on Tehran but US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Trump had not yet made a decision on fresh strikes.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Interior ministry says some 320,000 people protest across France as unrest flares</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0aa4a2ee7e8d02d67d0419e8b951391f326fba74dfb0a103f722e3677fadadb7</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T16:45:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261031-live-france-braces-for-halloween-protests-government-vows-tough-response--6825697d0a22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261031-live-france-braces-for-halloween-protests-government-vows-tough-response" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey nominates former foreign minister Sinirlioglu as UN chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30b7b0cfb79858b27361a99113a84f2ea9efcb5cd76bd88686f53bebd97d3817</id><updated>2026-11-01T15:18:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T14:28:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261031-turkey-nominates-former-foreign-minister-sinirlioglu-as-un-chief--8c6274edaf1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261031-turkey-nominates-former-foreign-minister-sinirlioglu-as-un-chief" /><summary type="html">Turkey has nominated its former foreign minister and UN ambassador Feridun Hadi Sinirlioglu for the position of UN secretary-general, state-media reported on Saturday. The submission was officially backed by Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan who has been particularly vocal in calling for reform of the UN Security Council.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
